---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /writing/
title: Writing
shortTitle: Writing
description: "Essays on evaluating AI systems: asymmetric thresholds, why aggregate metrics hide failures, judge independence, and reading your own production traffic."
---
<article class="page">
    <header class="page__header">
        {#
          Plain `.wrap`, not `.wrap--measure` — see layouts/page.njk for why.
          `.page__lede` already caps its own inline-size to the reading
          measure (article.css), so it reads at the right width while the
          header stays flush with the card grid below it.
        #}
        <div class="wrap">
            <h1 class="page__title">Writing</h1>
            <p class="page__lede">
                A case study answers "what did you build?". These answer "what should I do
                differently on Monday?". Each one is readable with no context about the platform I
                work on. The work is the worked example, not the subject.
            </p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap">
        <ul class="card-list card-list--posts">
            {% for item in collections.posts %}
            <li class="card card--post" data-reveal>
                <p class="card__eyebrow">
                    <time datetime="{{ item.date | isoDate }}">{{ item.date | readableDate }}</time>
                    <span data-volatile>{{ item.templateContent | readingTime }} min read</span>
                </p>
                {# h2, not h3. This list sits directly under the page h1 with no
                   section heading between them, so h3 would skip a level. #}
                <h2 class="card__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></h2>
                <p class="card__body">{{ item.data.description }}</p>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        {% if not collections.posts.length %}
        <p>Posts are being written. Check back shortly.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</article>
